---
import type { SidebarGroup } from '@/lib/content';
import { withBase } from '@/lib/url';
interface Props {
  groups: SidebarGroup[];
  headings: { slug: string }[];
}
const { groups, headings } = Astro.props;
const sectionIds = new Set(['badge-1-kit-bot', 'badge-2-intermediate-frc', 'badge-3-advanced-frc', 'how-a-badge-is-signed-off']);
---

{headings.filter(({ slug }) => !sectionIds.has(slug)).map(({ slug }) => <span id={slug} hidden />)}
<p>The Automation Badges are how FRC 4451's Automation Team tracks a student's progress from their first meeting to a working robot. Each badge has a printed packet with tasks, mentor signatures and any required worksheets.</p>
<p>The student should keep a notebook of notes, observations and questions. The lessons are intended to be completed in 30 to 60 minute sessions.</p>
{groups.map((group) => (
  <section>
    <h2 id={group.id === 'badge-1' ? 'badge-1-kit-bot' : group.id === 'badge-2' ? 'badge-2-intermediate-frc' : 'badge-3-advanced-frc'}>{group.label}</h2>
    {group.id !== 'badge-1' && <p>This badge curriculum is being revised.</p>}
    <ol>
      {group.items.map((item) => <li><a href={withBase(item.href)}>{item.label}</a></li>)}
    </ol>
  </section>
))}
<h2 id="how-a-badge-is-signed-off">How a Badge Is Signed Off</h2>
<p>For Badge 1, the student demonstrates each completed task to a mentor. The mentor signs a row after seeing its required evidence. The <a href={withBase('/badges/badge-1-sign-off')}>Badge 1 Sign-Off Sheet</a> lists the evidence for each row.</p>
